.\" zmake(1): the zmake command line. Keep in sync with src/cli.zig and
.\" docs/src/content/docs/docs/reference/cli.md (ADR-0027).
.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt ZMAKE 1
.Os zmake
.Sh NAME
.Nm zmake
.Nd Make-compatible build tool with a legacy mode and a modern mode
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar VAR Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Op Ar target ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads an input file and builds the targets on the command line.
It reads the input file in one of two modes.
.Pp
.Em Legacy mode
keeps strict POSIX and GNU Make semantics.
A target is a file unless
.Ic .PHONY
names it.
A recipe line starts with a tab.
.Pp
.Em Modern mode
removes the
.Ic .PHONY
boilerplate.
.Ic @name:
and
.Ic task name:
declare a task.
.Nm
infers a phony target from a bare name.
A recipe line starts with a tab or with two or more spaces.
.Pp
.Xr zmakefile 5
describes the two modes and the syntax of the input file.
.Pp
An argument with
.Ql =
sets a variable.
A command-line variable overrides the input file and the environment.
.Sh OPTIONS
Short options can share one argument, for example
.Fl kj4
or
.Fl sB .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar FILE , Fl -file Ns = Ns Ar FILE
Read
.Ar FILE
as the input file.
The basename selects the mode.
.It Fl C Ar DIR , Fl -directory Ns = Ns Ar DIR
Change to
.Ar DIR
before
.Nm
reads the input file.
.It Fl j Ar N , Fl j Ns Ar N , Fl -jobs Ns = Ns Ar N
Run up to
.Ar N
jobs at the same time.
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run , Fl -just-print
Print the recipe lines.
Do not run them.
.It Fl r , Fl -no-builtin-rules
Do not use the built-in implicit rules.
.It Fl R , Fl -no-builtin-variables
Do not define the built-in variables.
This option sets
.Fl r
too.
.It Fl k , Fl -keep-going
After a failure, build the other targets that do not need the failed target.
.It Fl q , Fl -question
Run nothing.
The exit status is 0 when the goals are up to date, else 1.
.It Fl t , Fl -touch
Set the time of each out-of-date file target to now.
Run no recipe.
.It Fl B , Fl -always-make
Treat every target as out of date.
.It Fl s , Fl -silent , Fl -quiet
Do not echo the recipe lines.
.It Fl -jobserver-style Ns = Ns Cm fifo | pipe
Set the style of a new jobserver.
The default is
.Cm pipe
on Linux and
.Cm fifo
on the other systems.
.It Fl -modern
Use modern mode for any input file.
.It Fl -legacy
Use legacy mode for any input file.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the version line and exit.
.Nm
reads no input file.
.El
.Ss Input file discovery
Without
.Fl f ,
.Nm
searches the directory in this order:
.Pa ZMakefile ,
.Pa Make.zig.mk ,
.Pa GNUmakefile ,
.Pa makefile ,
.Pa Makefile .
.Pa ZMakefile
and
.Pa Make.zig.mk
select modern mode.
The other names select legacy mode.
.Fl -modern
and
.Fl -legacy
override the file name.
.Ss Default goal
With no target on the command line,
.Nm
builds
.Va .DEFAULT_GOAL .
Without
.Va .DEFAULT_GOAL ,
it builds the first target that does not start with
.Ql \&.
and is not a pattern.
.Ss Recipe lines
Each recipe line runs in its own
.Ql /bin/sh -c .
A line can start with these prefixes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic @
Do not echo the line.
.It Ic -
Ignore a failure of the line.
.It Ic +
Run the line also under
.Fl n .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev MAKEFLAGS
.Nm
reads the flags of a parent make: the
.Cm B , k , n , q , r , R , s
and
.Cm t
flags,
.Fl j Ns Ar N ,
.Fl -jobserver-auth ,
.Fl -jobserver-fds
and the
.Ql -- VAR=value
overrides.
Each recipe line gets
.Ev MAKEFLAGS
with the same forms.
.It Ev MAKELEVEL
Each recipe line gets the value of the parent plus one.
.It Ev SHELL
.Nm
ignores
.Ev SHELL
from the environment.
Set
.Va SHELL
in the input file to change the shell.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Under
.Fl q :
a goal is not up to date.
.It 2
A usage error, a parse error, a missing rule, a cycle or a failed recipe line.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build the default goal with four jobs:
.Dl $ zmake -j4
.Pp
Show the recipe lines of the target
.Ar deploy
and run nothing:
.Dl $ zmake -n deploy
.Pp
Read a file with any name in modern mode:
.Dl $ zmake -f build.mk --modern
.Pp
Print the version and the git commit of the build:
.Dl $ zmake --version
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr zmakefile 5
.Pp
The full documentation is at
.Lk https://infrashift.github.io/zmake/
.Sh STANDARDS
In legacy mode,
.Nm
follows POSIX
.Xr make 1
and a defined subset of GNU Make 4.3.
It stops with an error for each feature outside this subset.
